{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Far away in sunny mountains, [G]where the [D]merry sunbeams play,[A]
[D]there I wandered thru the [G]clover, singing [A]to a village maid.[D]
[A]She was dearer than the dearest, [D]ever loving kind and true,[A]
[D]and she wore beneath her bonnet [G]amber [A]tresses tied in blue.[D]
{end_of_verse}

